@* The guesser's screen whenever they must see nothing yet. Not a UI convenience — the parent
   never even sends this viewer the word/clue text at these phases (JustOneSession.ViewFor), so
   there is nothing to accidentally leak here either.

   The progress line is safe for the same reason: a count of who has finished typing carries no
   information about the word or any clue, and without it the guesser is left staring at a
   frozen screen with no way to tell a busy table from a dead one. *@
<div class="card peek-shield">
    <div class="card-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Jij raadt deze ronde</p>
        <h1>🙈 @Message</h1>
        <p class="subtle">Jij mag het woord en de hints nog niet zien.</p>
    </div>

    @if (Total > 0)
    {
        <p class="jo-progress-count">@Submitted <span>/</span> @Total</p>
        <p class="timer-label">hints binnen</p>
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public string Message { get; set; } = "Wachten tot de anderen klaar zijn…";

    /// <summary>Zero disables the counter — used by the phases where nobody is typing.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public int Total { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public int Submitted { get; set; }
}
